#   guy --uninstall-hooks  remove GUY's hooks from it and nothing else
#   guy --activity ID ...  show a live activity from any script (guy --activity --help)
#   guy --listen           talk to GUY now (Super+Space); saying "Hey GUY" does the same (guy-voice)
#   guy --voice on|off     switch "Hey GUY" listening on or off (the microphone closes when off)
#
# Besides Claude Code it follows browser downloads (~/Downloads), pacman / yay as they run
# (/var/log/pacman.log), and the number of available updates (HyDE's `hyde-shell system.update`).
# Package runs pop the pill out at each step and let it slide back in; when yay / pacman / sudo sits
# waiting for you at a terminal (a password, [Y/n], a choice) it stays out until you've answered.
# Ask GUY also understands plain commands, done right away without asking Claude: "lower sound",
# "volume 30", "mute", "next song", "pause", "what's playing", "timer 25m", "remind me in 5 minutes
# to call mom", "cancel timer", and several at once ("lower sound and next song").

